  <h2>How affiliate compensation works</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on CryptoBonusWorld are affiliate or referral links. When a user registers through an approved link, the exchange may pay CryptoBonusWorld a commission under its partner program.
    Compensation can include revenue-share, CPA or hybrid arrangements. CryptoBonusWorld does not add a separate fee to the user's exchange account for using one of our referral links.
  </p>

  <h2>What affiliate relationships can affect</h2>
  <p>
    A commercial relationship can determine whether CryptoBonusWorld has an approved referral destination or an owner-confirmed promo code to display.
    It can also determine whether we can earn a commission from a particular registration route.
  </p>

  <h2>What affiliate relationships do not authorize</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p><strong>Affiliate status does not create a ranking position, country-availability claim, verified bonus amount or local offer eligibility.</strong></p>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li>A referral link does not prove that the exchange accepts residents of the active country.</li>
    <li>An owner-confirmed promo code does not prove a bonus amount, KYC requirement, deposit threshold, expiry date or account eligibility.</li>
    <li>A commercial partnership does not convert missing or stale evidence into a verified claim.</li>
    <li>The global Top 10 is not relabelled as a local ranking because of an affiliate relationship.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How affiliate links are identified</h2>
  <p>
    Approved exchange registration routes use governed internal paths such as <code>/go/bybit/</code> before sending the user to the confirmed exchange destination.
    Sponsored outbound actions are labelled accordingly in the page markup. The exchange controls the destination account flow and its final terms.
  </p>

  <h2>About bonus and offer claims</h2>
  <p>
    Advertised rewards can be conditional and may vary by campaign, account status and location. A headline maximum is not a guaranteed payment.
    Where a claim is not currently supported by accepted evidence, CryptoBonusWorld keeps it under review rather than using the commercial relationship as proof.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
  <p>Before registering or depositing, verify the current exchange-owned terms, your country eligibility, product availability and any campaign requirements that apply to your account.</p>

  <h2>Editorial standards and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>, <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> and
    <a href="/update-policy/">Update Policy</a> for how evidence, ranking and freshness are handled.
    To report a problem or ask about a commercial relationship, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout legal-callout--risk">
    <p>CryptoBonusWorld provides informational comparison content. Nothing on the site is financial, investment, legal or tax advice. Cryptocurrency trading involves substantial risk.</p>
  </div>
